Student(sid, name, major)
Course(cid, title, dept)
Enroll(sid, cid, quarter)
Required(major, cid)


//1
π name (
  σ major = 'CS' (Student)
)

select name from student where name is CS


π name, title (
  (Student ⋈ Student.sid = Enroll.sid Enroll)
  ⋈ Enroll.cid = Course.cid Course
)

get the name and title of each student and the course that it is enrolled in



π name, title (
  (σ major = 'CS' (Student) ⋈ Student.sid = Enroll.sid Enroll)
  ⋈ Enroll.cid = Course.cid
  (σ dept = 'CSE' (Course))
)
gets the name, course title of students that are CS majors and enrolled in classes that are in CSE department


π sid (Student)
−
π sid (Enroll)

get all students that are not enrolled in any



π sid, name (Student)
−
π Student.sid, name (
  Student ⋈ Student.sid = Enroll.sid Enroll
)
get all sid, names of students who never enrolled in any course



π sid (σ major = 'CS' (Student))
∪
π sid (σ major = 'Math' (Student))

get all students who are cs majors or math majors


π name, title (
  Student × Course
)
returns every possible combination of student names and course titles


Student ⋈ Student.sid = Enroll.sid Enroll
σ Student.sid = Enroll.sid (Student × Enroll)

they are the same!
First form: explicit join (preferred, cleaner, more efficient)
Second form: create all pairs first, then filter (conceptual definition of join)


Student ⋈ Enroll
What condition is implicitly used in this natural join?
they see equality of attrs with same name: student.sid = enroll.sid


π sid (Student)
−
ρ sid (π student_id (OldEnroll))
Why is the rename needed?
it is selecting all sid from student and excepting using old enroll
we rename to match sid to student_id in OldEnroll


Sailor(sname, rating)
Boat(bname, rating)
Reservation(sname, bname, day)
Weekday(day)

π Reservation.bname (
  (Reservation ⋈ Reservation.sname = Sailor.sname Sailor)
  ⋈ Sailor.rating >= Boat.rating ∧ Reservation.bname = Boat.bname Boat
)
get all boats that are reserved by atleast one sailor who are qualified

π Reservation.sname, Reservation.bname, day (
  (Reservation ⋈ Reservation.sname = Sailor.sname Sailor)
  ⋈ Reservation.bname = Boat.bname ∧ Sailor.rating < Boat.rating Boat
)
get sailors name and boat name where the sailor cant sail the boat


Wong-Youssefi / Simple RA Plan Writing

SELECT s.name, c.title
FROM Student s, Enroll e, Course c
WHERE s.sid = e.sid
  AND e.cid = c.cid
  AND s.major = 'CS'
  AND c.dept = 'CSE';

optimized RA:
  π s.name, c.title
(
  (σ major = 'CS' (Student))
  ⋈ Student.sid = Enroll.sid
  (
    Enroll
    ⋈ Enroll.cid = Course.cid
    (σ dept = 'CSE' (Course))
  )
)
Filter Student early (major = CS)
Filter Course early (dept = CSE)
Join smaller relations first

